Marlowe — first run under this profile. What it can reach:

  FILES
    C:\Users\matth\AppData\Local\Temp\m3demo/ws
    That directory and everything under it. Nothing outside it: paths are resolved and checked before opening, and symlinks pointing out are refused.

  NETWORK
    Nothing, until you approve a host. Every fetch asks, and every fetch asks again — approvals are not remembered between requests in this build.
    A fetched page is read by a separate, sandboxed process that holds no tools; only a short summary of it comes back.

  MEMORY
    WRITE-ONLY · no --reranking directory; the rank-1/rank-2 margin the declared operating point reads does not exist without a cross-encoder
    What you tell Marlowe can be written to a signed journal on this machine, under the profile directory. It is not sent anywhere.

  ALWAYS ASKS YOU FIRST
    bash     Run a command through the Windows shell, `cmd /C` — NOT bash, despite the name.
    (and any network request, per host, every time)

  MAY ACT WITHOUT ASKING
    ask      Put a question to the user and wait.
    edit     Replace a file's contents, or write a new file.
    find     Search files under a directory for a literal substring, line by line.
    read     Read a file in the workspace by workspace-relative `path`, OR a fetched document by `ref` (the id `web` returns).
    recall   Search Marlowe's own memory: what the user said in earlier sessions, and what Marlowe has learned.
    remember Ask the harness to record something worth keeping.
    run      Delegate a sub-task to a child run.
    use      Find and load a skill.
    web      Fetch one URL over https and return the page.
    Whether these ask depends on the trust tier this run was granted. The trust ledger that would raise a tier does not exist yet, so today they run at the tier the profile starts with.

  The model chooses what to do; the harness decides what it is allowed to do, and the decisions are in the journal.

